      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Le_Raysville%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough’s Main Street doubles as State Route 467, winding north‑south through the heart of LeRaysville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.bradfordcountypa.gov/212/LeRaysville-Borough"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "LeRaysville was carved out of Pike Township in 1863, becoming an independent borough that year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.bradfordcountypa.gov/212/LeRaysville-Borough"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Two streams, Ford Street Creek and Rockwell Creek, run through LeRaysville, feeding its modest waterways.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
